1
00:00:15,900 --> 00:00:16,903
SULLIVAN: Ask me.

2
00:00:16,953 --> 00:00:17,544
REYES: Ask you.

3
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:31,041
A watch turnover takes fifteen minutes.

4
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,951
A career takes fifteen years.

5
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:43,423
Most of what makes a senior person valuable
never gets written down. Who to call.

6
00:00:43,473 --> 00:00:49,595
Which alarm always lies. Why the
workaround from 2019 is still there.

7
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:55,910
And when they rotate, retire or transfer,
it walks out the gate with them.

8
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:07,666
What if the job could be handed over the whole way, with
her consent, from her first week to her last?

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,365
The Long Turnover is a way to capture it.
With her consent. On her machine.

10
00:01:16,415 --> 00:01:20,162
Anonymized, then distilled by generative
models.

11
00:01:20,212 --> 00:01:22,677
And counted only once she confirms it.

12
00:01:23,477 --> 00:01:28,959
Not a surveillance product. An agent she
helps build, and signs.

13
00:01:30,477 --> 00:01:35,449
It has a service record. It shadows. It
co-pilots.

14
00:01:35,499 --> 00:01:39,011
It sits sea trials against her own past
cases.

15
00:01:39,061 --> 00:01:43,389
It relieves her, and it advises, but a
human decides.

16
00:01:43,439 --> 00:01:47,574
Then it goes emeritus, with the date of
its knowledge on every answer.

17
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:51,048
And one day it is decommissioned, on
purpose.

18
00:01:51,848 --> 00:01:55,943
Opt-in. Revocable. Never used to rate or
rank her.

19
00:01:55,993 --> 00:02:01,169
Anonymized before any model sees it. Every
claim traced to its source.

20
00:02:01,219 --> 00:02:06,500
A named human decides. And her name stays
on what she taught it.

21
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:12,838
Passive capture is good at what people do.
It is poor at why.

22
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:20,543
The why lives in the hard calls, and she
does not know which ones mattered.

23
00:02:20,593 --> 00:02:21,987
Neither does the system.

24
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,166
So we ask a different question.

25
00:02:26,366 --> 00:02:29,668
Can wearable sensors tell us when a hard
decision is being made?

26
00:02:29,718 --> 00:02:32,259
Not what she is thinking. When.

27
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:38,085
The sensor only picks the moment. The
answer is hers.

28
00:02:38,135 --> 00:02:40,332
SULLIVAN: That one, yes. Here is why.

29
00:02:40,382 --> 00:02:47,505
The sensors never read thoughts, never judge skill, and
the raw signals are deleted after each session.

30
00:02:52,305 --> 00:02:58,478
Phase one is small on purpose. Ninety
days. Four developer volunteers.

31
00:02:58,528 --> 00:03:02,476
Two veteran-and-successor pairs, in an
isolated lab.

32
00:03:02,526 --> 00:03:04,985
Nothing identifiable leaves the building.

33
00:03:05,785 --> 00:03:07,635
Setup. Calibration.

34
00:03:07,685 --> 00:03:12,640
Real work, with questions timed by sensors
against questions on a schedule.

35
00:03:12,690 --> 00:03:18,656
And a successor test: can the next person finish the
veteran's task using only what was captured?

36
00:03:19,456 --> 00:03:21,753
Five questions, each with a measure.

37
00:03:32,056 --> 00:03:37,742
The request is equipment only: about seven
and a half to eight thousand dollars.

38
00:03:37,792 --> 00:03:40,127
Labor is the team's own time.

39
00:03:40,927 --> 00:03:44,828
It ends in one of three ways. Go: field
pilot.

40
00:03:44,878 --> 00:03:48,550
Pivot: keep the headsets, drop the extra
sensors.

41
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:54,102
Stop: keep the weekly questions, no
sensors. Each outcome is useful.

42
00:03:54,902 --> 00:04:05,466
If it works, the road runs on: a field pilot, a software relief agent, and, years
away, a robot that carries the expert's judgment as well as their motions.

43
00:04:06,166 --> 00:04:09,063
Always with a named person accountable.

44
00:04:10,366 --> 00:04:13,079
This part is not part of this request.

45
00:04:14,466 --> 00:04:20,689
We are asking for four decisions. Fund the
equipment. Approve the quote request.

46
00:04:20,789 --> 00:04:23,326
Approve a ninety-day study with
volunteers.

47
00:04:23,426 --> 00:04:27,306
And name the people who will hold us to
our own guardrails.

48
00:04:32,706 --> 00:04:41,335
RELIEF: Loop 4. In winter this alarm is a known false trigger. Confirmed by
Chief Sullivan, eleven months ago. Please verify before you ignore it.

49
00:04:42,406 --> 00:04:45,094
A watch turnover takes fifteen minutes.

50
00:04:46,006 --> 00:04:50,601
A career takes fifteen years. Hand it over
the whole way.

51
00:04:52,601 --> 00:04:54,081
Let's start now.
